      "title": "Puerto Rican Chicken Fricassée + white rice + green salad",
      "do": "Start by 4:30pm. Toss chicken with adobo, 3 Tbsp mashed garlic, 2 Tbsp olive oil, turmeric, extra oregano, ground coriander; refrigerate 30 min. Brown chicken in 1 Tbsp oil in a heavy pot; set aside; add 1 Tbsp oil, onion, bell pepper, cilantro; sauté 4 min. Deglaze with red wine; stir in diced tomato + tomato paste. Return chicken with bay leaves, extra olives, potatoes, carrots; boil, then cover and simmer 45 min; uncover and simmer 15 min to thicken. Cook rice; toss salad greens with olive oil + vinegar.",
